cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below. The paper will be the preferred citation once it is released."
title: "cpilens: multilingual classification of Thai product text for consumer price measurement"
abstract: >-
  Multilingual classification of Thai product text into the items of the Thai
  consumer price index, evaluated on held-out official specifications with
  CPI-expenditure weights, and an inflation simulator that turns each method's confusion matrix
  into basis points of measured inflation. Public data only. Code: MIT. Data
  derived from Open Food Facts: ODbL 1.0.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chongmankhong
    given-names: Thanatchon
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23686886
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/thanatchon36/cpilens"
keywords:
  - consumer price index
  - product classification
  - multilingual text embeddings
  - large language models
  - inflation measurement
  - Thailand
